`std::transform` is Python's `[f(x) for x in xs]`. It writes where its output iterator points and never grows a vector.

```cpp
std::vector<double> px{100.0, 102.0, 99.0};
std::vector<double> pence;
std::transform(px.begin(), px.end(), pence.begin(),
               [](double p) { return p * 100; });
```

